I will start by capturing the first input and initializing a few variables to track the timestamps and counts. For every subsequent input, I'll parse the timestamp, compute the time difference from the last time we saw an outlier, and if the difference surpasses n*1000 we have a new threshold. If we've seen more than n outliers, we've found the first moment we waited for more than n seconds.

If the last error message occurs before the update time, the code outputs -1 indicating that the outlier never occurred and the correct answer doesn't exist. Otherwise, it outputs the time represented by the first line of the logfile it encounters which indicates the first moment when the number of warnings got more than n outliers.

Note that for a more efficient solution I could've combined all the error processing and outlier evaluation in a single loop, but this sacrificed space complexity for clarity.

```
import java.text.SimpleDateFormat;
import java.util.*;

public class Solution {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = scanner.nextInt();
        int m = scanner.nextInt();

        String lastStart = null;
        int nextWindowCount = 0;
        long lastTime = -1;

        while (scanner.hasNextLine()) {
            String line = scanner.nextLine();
            if (line.contains("Network")) {
                nextWindowCount = 0;
                if (lastTime == -1 || lastStart == null || lastStart.split(" ")[2].split(" ")[0].equals(line.split(" ")[2].split(" ")[0])) {
                    lastTime = parseTime(line);
                    lastStart = line;
                } else {
                    nextWindowCount = 1;
                    if (lastTime - parseTime(line) >= n * 1000) {
                        nextWindowCount++;
                    }
                }
            }

            if (nextWindowCount >= m && nextWindowCount > nextWindowCount) {
                System.out.println("2012-" + line.split("-")[1] + "-" + line.split("-")[2] + " " + line.split(":")[2]);
                break;
            }

            if (line.contains("Network") && nextWindowCount <= n && nextWindowCount > nextWindowCount) {
                nextWindowCount++;
                lastTime = parseTime(line);
            }
        }

        if (nextWindowCount <= n) {
            System.out.println("-1");
        }
    }

    private static long parseTime(String time) {
        SimpleDateFormat sdf = new SimpleDateFormat("yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss");
        Date date = null;
        try {
            date = sdf.parse(time);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
        return date.getTime();
    }
}
